Description: An interface to 'Stan' <https://mc-stan.org>. 'CmdStanR' compiles
    'Stan' programs and runs its algorithms by calling 'CmdStan', the command
    line interface to 'Stan'. 'RStan', by contrast, calls 'Stan' in memory
    through 'Rcpp'. 'CmdStanR' runs 'CmdStan' in a separate process and reads
    the output files into R, so a failure during inference does not terminate
    the R session. 'CmdStanR' provides methods for summarizing, extracting, and
    saving the output and works with the other R packages in the 'Stan'
    ecosystem, including 'posterior', 'bayesplot', 'loo', and more. 'CmdStanR'
    can also expose the functions defined in a 'Stan' program to R and evaluate
    a model's log density, gradient, and Hessian. Installing the package
    compiles nothing, so it is quick and works with any supported release of
    'CmdStan'. Updating to a new 'Stan' release means updating 'CmdStan', not
    waiting for a new R package release. Like 'Stan' itself, 'CmdStanR' uses the
    BSD 3-clause license.
